{
  "id": "grammar.a1.03c.04.noun-adjective",
  "title": "People I Know",
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Noun + adjective",
      "content": "You can identify a person with ser + a noun phrase and then describe them. The article, noun and adjective agree: un hombre alto, una mujer alta."
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Basic combinations",
      "rows": [
        [
          "un hombre",
          "un hombre alto"
        ],
        [
          "una mujer",
          "una mujer alta"
        ],
        [
          "un chico",
          "un chico joven"
        ],
        [
          "una persona",
          "una persona amable"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "examples",
      "items": [
        {
          "spanish": "Carlos es un hombre alto.",
          "english": "Carlos is a tall man."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Ana es una mujer simpática.",
          "english": "Ana is a friendly woman."
        },
        {
          "spanish": "Meg es una persona amable.",
          "english": "Meg is a kind person."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "tip",
      "content": "The adjective agrees with the noun it describes. This lesson combines article and noun knowledge from earlier units with adjective agreement. For further reference, see Lingolia's Spanish adjective reference."
    }
  ]
}